1
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:06,040
Reading Journey Down the Mekong

2
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:12,700
Part 1 The Dream and the Plan My name is Wang Kun.

3
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:14,720
Ever since middle school,

4
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:19,120
my sister Wang Wei and I have dreamed about taking a great bike trip.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,460
Two years ago she bought an expensive mountain bike and then she persuaded me to buy one.

6
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:47,260
Wang Wei soon got them interested in cycling too.

7
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:53,000
After graduating from college, we finally got the chance to take a bike trip.

8
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:56,260
I asked my sister, "Where are we going?"

9
00:00:56,860 --> 00:01:03,020
It was my sister who first had the idea to cycle along the entire Mekong River from where

10
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:04,900
it begins to where it ends.

11
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:13,520
I am fond of my sister but she has one serious shortcoming.

12
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:15,740
She can be really stubborn.

13
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:19,860
Although she didn’t know the best way of getting to places,

14
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:23,700
she insisted that she organize the trip properly.

15
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:29,140
Now I know that the proper way is always her way.

16
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:34,580
I kept asking her, "When are we leaving and when are we coming back?"

17
00:01:35,140 --> 00:01:38,100
I asked her whether she had looked at a map yet.

18
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:42,840
Of course she hadn’t; my sister doesn’t care about details.

19
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:48,160
So I told her that the source of the Mekong is in Qinghai Province.

20
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:54,580
She gave me a determined look - the kind that said she would not change her mind.

21
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:08,700
When I told her the air would be hard to breathe and it would be very cold,

22
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:11,600
she said it would be an interesting experience.

23
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:14,080
I know my sister well.

24
00:02:14,610 --> 00:02:18,380
Once she has made up her mind, nothing can change it.

25
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:21,340
Finally, I had to give in.

26
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:23,740
Several months before our trip,

27
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:26,320
Wang Wei and I went to the library.

28
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:32,440
We found a large atlas with good maps that showed details of world geography.

29
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:39,560
From the atlas we could see that the Mekong River begins in a glacier on a Tibetan mountain.

30
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:44,800
At first the river is small and the water is clear and cold.

31
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:47,340
Then it begins to move quickly.

32
00:03:06,110 --> 00:03:08,800
After it leaves China and high altitude,

33
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:12,940
the Mekong becomes wide, brown and warm.

34
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:16,980
As it enters Southeast Asia, its pace slows.

35
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:22,560
It makes wide bends or meanders through low valleys to the plains where

36
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:23,480
rice grows.
